<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Drabya Shah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1570">1570</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Drabya Shah was the founder of the Gorkha Kingdom in the hills of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>. A younger son of the ruler of Lamjung, he seized Gorkha in 1559 from its Khadka chief and became its first king of the Shah dynasty. His descendant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prithvi-narayan-shah">Prithvi Narayan Shah</a> conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu-valley">Kathmandu Valley</a> in the 18th century and created the modern kingdom of Nepal.</p></div>
